{
  "dom_id": "step-q85316",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n\n- The number of visits a web page has per minute\n- The number of works of art created by a sculptor in a period of one year\n- The average height of the players on a basketball team",
  "worked_solution": "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I follows a Poisson distribution. The number of visits on a web page can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a minute).\n\n- Random variable II follows a Poisson distribution. The number of works of art can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a year).\n\n- Random variable III does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of time or space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
