  "html": "<div id=\"step-q85316\" class=\"step questionWidget\" style=\"display: block;\"><div class=\"questionWidget-header\"><div class=\"questionWidget-title\">Question 3</div><div class=\"questionWidget-helpButton\">?</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-text\"><p>Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  The number of visits a web page has per minute </li><li>  The number of works of art created by a sculptor in a period of one year </li><li>  The average height of the players on a basketball team </li></ol></div><table class=\"questionWidget-choicesTable\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-85316-a\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">a</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-85316-b\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">b</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">III only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-85316-c\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">c</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and III only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-85316-d\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">d</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I, II, and III</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-85316-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\" style=\"background: rgb(64, 64, 64); color: white;\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and II only</td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.</p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Random variable I follows a Poisson distribution. The number of visits on a web page can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a minute).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Random variable II follows a Poisson distribution. The number of works of art can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a year).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Random variable III does <em>not</em> follow a Poisson distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of time or space.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
